As a variant on the normal challenge, I thought I'd try to see how
quickly I could ascend in wizard mode (a la the tool-assisted speed
runs you see on the internet for NES games, et cetera). There are a few
variants worth exploring, I think:

* No wishing for key items (ritual artifacts, Amulet)
* No death
* No wishing for key items *and* no death
* No rules whatsoever

I only had time for a quick game today, so I tried a no-rules speed run
and ascended in 65 turns, dying thirteen times. I'm sure that could be
knocked down to 50 or so, but it was pretty good for a first attempt
IMO. (Actually, my first attempt involved wishing for a magic portal on
the Plane of Earth, but it turns out that stepping on it will mess up
your game.) I used +127 boots of speed to get bonus turns and the Magic
Mirror of Merlin for telepathy on the Astral Plane.

Anyone beat that? Ever tried something like this? It's an interesting
twist on the normal challenge of the game, I think.



